A||||10||jlruiz67||Best tire size for stock rims?||||5||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||10-29-2000||01:06 PM||||Hello all <BR>   I like to know what is the best price vs performance vs size for stock 15" rims on my 87 GT front and rear. I think I'm one of the few that acturally likes the stock rims on my GT. I was thinking on going 215-50-15 on front and 225-50-15 rear with a lowering kit,I like to know what would be a good brand and model and if anyone knows how big can I go on the rear. Thank you much.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||10-29-2000||02:13 PM||||I have a set of BFGoodrich 225/50R15 Euro T/A's on a set of GT wheels. These are mounted on my lowered 1986 SE. I have no rubbing problems and it handles like it's glued to the road!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1986SE.jpg">  <P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||10-29-2000||08:00 PM||||Oreif:  Are those actual lace wheels from a GT?  I would think that 50s would be too big for the rims.  I am thinking of using 205/60-15s on the front, then maybe 225/50-15s on the rear.  Would this cause any problems?  I would use 50s on the front, but I want to have a wider tire on the rear.  So, is this possible?  It would make sense, since you have them.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-29-2000||08:39 PM||||The previous owner of my 88 put 225/60-15's on the front and 235/60's on the back. It is too much tire for the wheel, especially on the back. The rear tires look like they're pulled in by the wheel. I am putting stock sizes back on it- already got 205's on the front and next month (hopefully) will put some 215's on the back.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-29-2000||08:47 PM||||Why would 50's be too big? If anything it would be too small. The first number in a tire marking is the width of the tire in mm, at its widest point. The second number is the aspect ratio. Meaning the side wall is 50% or 60% of width. The last number is the rim size it mounts to. If you use 50's on the rear and 60's on the front, your front tires are going to be bigger then the rears. The rears will be wider, but smaller. Using anything but 205/60R15 on the front will throw the speedo off.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/singnit.gif"> <BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||10-29-2000||08:55 PM||||Yes, they are 87 GT lace wheels. I refinished them in black. The 225/50R15's will fit a 6" to 8" wide wheel per BFGoodrich's site. As for wheel diameter the 60 series tire will be higher so putting 60's on the front and 50's in the rear will raise the front of the car. As for speedo, My original tire size was 215/60R14 so going to a 225/50R15 only affects my speedo by 1.2% slower. Also ONLY the rear tire will affect speedo readings. (This is where the  speed sensor is) Check out the below link to find speedo error and actual tire measurements like diameter.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bill H||10-29-2000||09:28 PM|||| Hey Oreif where did you get that air intake I love it. It must cool things down alot back there.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||10-29-2000||10:16 PM||||The Indy Fiero Over-the-roof scoop was bought thru IRM. It works great! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||jlruiz67||12-08-2000||09:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>I have a set of BFGoodrich 225/50R15 Euro T/A's on a set of GT wheels. These are mounted on my lowered 1986 SE. I have no rubbing problems and it handles like it's glued to the road!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1986SE.jpg">   <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank you very much for the advice, I just got the tires mounted and a 4 weel alingment. Boy what a difference I wasn't to sure about the tire size but your right it does feel better, they stick alot beter and I'm speeding with confidence once more.<P>||||reg||1
